Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:50:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] T4: add weighted final grade

- local\grade_calculator (pure functions) calculates the grade when
  weighting and/or numeric grading are enabled; with both disabled the
  upstream get_grade() code runs unchanged.
- With weighting every criterion is normalised and averaged with its
  weight, keeping the lockzeropoints semantics. Without weighting the
  upstream formulas apply.
- Criteria that cannot be normalised are left out, a criterion without
  filling counts 0, rounding and scales work as upstream.
- With numeric grading get_min_max_score() returns a minimum of 0, so the
  zero levels warning and the mapping explanation match the ranges.
- Replaces the provisional numeric branch added to get_grade() in T2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
